# Routing replay (MoE routed experts) openbox verification script.
#
# Adapted from vllm-ascend e2e test:
#   tests/e2e/pull_request/two_card/rlhf/consistency/test_moe_routing_replay.py
#
# Differences from the upstream e2e test:
#   * This script runs as a standalone CLI, NOT a pytest case.
#   * It accepts the **baseline launch command** (the `vllm serve ...` command
#     auto-generated by the model-rl-case-guard skill, which carries the model
#     path + TP/DP/EP/graph-mode topology).
#   * Verification runs in TWO steps (both required by the skill):
#       1. http  : start the baseline command as an HTTP `vllm serve`, then POST
#                  a completion and validate `choices[].routed_experts`
#                  (base64 -> np.load).
#       2. inproc: parse the parallel params out of the baseline command, build
#                  an in-process `VllmRunner` with --enable-return-routed-experts,
#                  then read `outputs[0].outputs[0].routed_experts` tensor.
#
# Usage (the skill agent invokes it with the baseline command it generated):
#
#   python test_moe_routing_replay.py \
#       --baseline-cmd "vllm serve /path/to/model --tensor-parallel-size 2 \
#                       --data-parallel-size 2 --enable-expert-parallel \
#                       --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\": \"FULL_DECODE_ONLY\"}' --port 8000" \
#       [--verify-mode http|inproc|both]   (default: both)
#       [--port 8000]               (used for http mode; default parsed from baseline cmd or 8000)
#       [--host 127.0.0.1]
#
# Exit code 0 == both verification steps passed; non-zero otherwise.

